{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 30, "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}, "title": "nvkvm: an NVIDIA GPU inside a KVM guest"}
[0.010154, "o", "\u001b[1;37mnvkvm -- an NVIDIA GPU inside a KVM guest.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;37mNo VFIO, no passthrough: the host keeps using the card the whole time.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.010154, "o", "\u001b[1;32mhost \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36m$ nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,driver_version,memory.total --format=csv,noheader\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.010154, "o", "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU, 580.173.02, 4096 MiB\r\n"]
[2.012675, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.514852, "o", "\u001b[1;32mhost \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36m$ lspci -k -d 10de: | head -3\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.929345, "o", "0000:01:00.0 VGA compatible controller: NVIDIA Corporation GA107M [GeForce RTX 3050 Mobile] (rev a1)\r\n\tSubsystem: ASUSTeK Computer Inc. GA107M [GeForce RTX 3050 Mobile]\r\n\tKernel driver in use: nvidia\r\n"]
[2.929349, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.430929, "o", "\u001b[1;32mhost \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36m$ scripts/run_test_vm.sh\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.430929, "o", "INFO: Using patched QEMU at /opt/qemu-nvkvm/bin/qemu-system-x86_64\r\nStarting nvkvm test VM...\r\nQEMU         : /opt/qemu-nvkvm/bin/qemu-system-x86_64\r\nDisk image   : /opt/nvkvm-guest/ubuntu-24.04.qcow2\r\nSeed ISO     : /opt/nvkvm-guest/seed.iso\r\nRepo (9p)    : /root/nvkvm  \u2192  guest:/mnt/nvkvm  (tag: nvkvm_src)\r\nSSH          : ssh ubuntu@localhost -p 2222\r\n\r\nnvkvm: host driver 580.173.02 \u2192 ABI profile 580\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: warning: nvkvm: isolate sandbox: uid+chroot (uid window 500000..504095, 4096 slots)\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: warning: nvkvm: isolate mode auto: 'namespace' UNAVAILABLE \u2014 clone(CLONE_NEWUSER|CLONE_NEWPID|CLONE_NEWNET|CLONE_NEWIPC|CLONE_NEWUTS|CLONE_NEWNS) failed: Operation not permitted. Typical under the default Docker seccomp/AppArmor profile, which blocks CLONE_NEWUSER regardless of kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone and user.max_user_namespaces.\r\nisolate mode auto -> uid+chroot. CAP_SYS_CHROOT is present, so chroot(\"/dev\") confinement is included. This is a MATERIALLY WEAKER boundary than namespace mode: no pid, mount, net, ipc or uts isolation. See docs/internal/isolate-model.md before relying on it.\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: warning: nvkvm: this is WEAKER than the default 'namespace' isolation \u2014 see docs/internal/isolate-model.md\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: info: nvkvm: GPA width: host MAXPHYADDR 39 bits, guest MAXPHYADDR 39 bits -> using 39 bits (limit 0x8000000000, 512 GiB)\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: info: nvkvm: GPA windows: guest RAM top ~0x280000000 (10 GiB), floor 0x2000000000 -> block base 0x5bc0000000 size 81 GiB [shm 0x5bc0000000, mmap 0x5c00000000 +16 GiB, sparse 0x6000000000 +64 GiB] (SPARSE WINDOW SHRUNK)\r\nqemu-system-x86_64: -device virtio-nvgpu-pci-non-transitional: warning: nvkvm: the sparse GPA window was reduced to 64 GiB (from 128 GiB) to fit this VM's 39-bit address space; a single cuCtxCreate issues >1500 mmaps, so very large GPU working sets may exhaust it\r\nnvkvm present: registered QemuConsole for guest GPU scanout (window display)\r\n[    0.000000] Linux version 6.8.0-138-generic (buildd@lcy02-amd64-023) (x86_64-linux-gnu-gcc-13 (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0, GNU ld (GNU Binutils for Ubuntu) 2.42) #138-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Jul 31 22:41:49 UTC 2026 (Ubuntu 6.8.0-138.138-generic 6.8.12)\r\r\n[    0.000000] Command line: BOOT_IMAGE=/vmlinuz-6.8.0-138-generic root=UUID=92327a9a-dabf-4d28-a338-bc96b268f068 ro console=tty1 console=ttyS0\r\r\n[    0.000000] KERNEL supported cpus:\r\r\n[    0.000000]   Intel GenuineIntel\r\r\n[    0.000000]   AMD AuthenticAMD\r\r\n[    0.000000]   Hygon HygonGenuine\r\r\n[    0.000000]   Centaur CentaurHauls\r\r\n[    0.000000]   zhaoxin   Shanghai  \r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-provided physical RAM map:\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x0000000000000000-0x000000000009fbff] usable\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x000000000009fc00-0x000000000009ffff] reserved\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x00000000000f0000-0x00000000000fffff] reserved\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x0000000000100000-0x00000000bffd9fff] usable\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x00000000bffda000-0x00000000bfffffff] reserved\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x00000000feffc000-0x00000000feffffff] reserved\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x00000000fffc0000-0x00000000ffffffff] reserved\r\r\n[    0.000000] BIOS-e820: [mem 0x0000000100000000-0x00000001bfffffff] usable\r\r\n[    0.000000] NX (Execute Disable) protection: active\r\r\n[    0.000000] APIC: Static calls initialized\r\r\n[    0.000000] SMBIOS 2.8 present.\r\r\n[    0.000000] DMI: QEMU Standard PC (i440FX + PIIX, 1996), BIOS rel-1.16.3-0-ga6ed6b701f0a-prebuilt.qemu.org 04/01/2014\r\r\n[    0.000000] Hypervisor detected: KVM\r\r\n[  